Subject: [PATCH] k60: define the SPI availability family in EXTERNAL_HEADERS

The 27 tree's EXTERNAL_HEADERS/Availability.h predates __SPI_AVAILABLE.
prepare-xnu.py copies it into the fakeroot on every run, so the define has to
live in the tree; libsyscall/wrappers/gethostuuid.h:41 is the first caller.

Generated against xnu ac9718f.
---
--- a/EXTERNAL_HEADERS/Availability.h
+++ b/EXTERNAL_HEADERS/Availability.h
@@ -418,3 +418,20 @@
 #define __API_UNAVAILABLE(...) __API_UNAVAILABLE_GET_MACRO(__VA_ARGS__,__API_UNAVAILABLE3,__API_UNAVAILABLE2,__API_UNAVAILABLE1)(__VA_ARGS__)
 
 #endif /* __AVAILABILITY__ */
+
+/* Added for the K60 port: this Availability.h predates the SPI availability
+   family, and libsyscall/wrappers/gethostuuid.h calls __SPI_AVAILABLE. Undefined,
+   that macro expands to a parenthesised list after a declarator, which is a parse
+   error rather than a missing attribute; availability attributes carry no codegen
+   effect, so defining the family empty is the correct repair. Kept in the tree
+   rather than patched into the fakeroot because prepare-xnu.py re-copies this
+   header on every run. */
+#ifndef __SPI_AVAILABLE
+#define __SPI_AVAILABLE(...)
+#endif
+#ifndef __SPI_DEPRECATED
+#define __SPI_DEPRECATED(...)
+#endif
+#ifndef __SPI_DEPRECATED_WITH_REPLACEMENT
+#define __SPI_DEPRECATED_WITH_REPLACEMENT(...)
+#endif
